TGDATA_ADD("g-rules",{"guide":{"game_rules":{"intro":"Each line names its source. Lines from another server or from one player are labelled.","cards":[{"id":"anniv2-group-buy","top":true,"title":"2nd Anniversary Value Group Buy: every round left","intro":"The event runs November 10 to November 24, 2026 (it ends at 8:00 AM US Eastern). This is the full list from the game's own event table, so you can save Diamonds for the rounds that matter.","lines":[{"text":"Rounds start at 05:00 or 17:00 server time. On our server that is 8:00 AM and 8:00 PM US Eastern. A round marked \"first half\" or \"second half\" lasts 12 hours; the others last 24.","source":"game event table ActGroupBuy_Anniv_2nd (Broken Chains copy of the game tables, pulled November 4, 2026) (round lengths); the Eastern times come from the in-game countdown on November 16, 2026"},{"text":"You pay the price shown when you buy. When more players buy, the price drops, and the game mails you the difference when the round ends. So buying early costs nothing extra.","source":"game rule text Anni2ndGroupBuy_RuleDesc_1_1_2 and 1_1_3"},{"text":"Have up to 90% of the full price on hand when you buy: the first discount is 10%, and the rest only comes back by mail after the round. One of our players paid 45,000 for round 10 (full price 50,000, lowest price 30,000).","source":"game event table ActGroupBuy_Anniv_2nd (Broken Chains copy of the game tables, pulled November 4, 2026) (field discount: the first step is 0.9 from 0 purchases); the 45,000 is a player report, TGBTC Discord, November 16, 2026"},{"text":"Plan with the lowest price. The last discount step needs 5,000 purchases (we think per server), and the event table has the game add purchases to that count by itself during each round. A player expected round 10 to end at 30,000, its lowest price. (our reading of the game data)","source":"game event table ActGroupBuy_Anniv_2nd (Broken Chains copy of the game tables, pulled November 4, 2026) (fields discount, discount_count and auto_stop); a player on an older server, TGBTC Discord, November 16, 2026"},{"text":"Record (our call of November 17, these rounds have ended): Must-buys left: the LR Tactic Random Chest on November 19 and the Promotion Stone caskets on November 21. Together they cost 12,300 Diamonds at the lowest price (have 13,500 on hand for the chest and 3,240 for the caskets if you buy early). Free players: buy these two and stop. Tactics are probably usable only from about server day 60 (unconfirmed), so the chest is one to buy and hold.","source":"our call from the prices in game event table ActGroupBuy_Anniv_2nd (Broken Chains copy of the game tables, pulled November 4, 2026); both are also \"Buy 100%\" in a buy list shared by another org (screenshot in the TGBTC Discord, November 16, 2026); day 60: game setting SeniorArenaTacticUnlockDays = 60 (Strategic Arena Tactics) and a player on an older server, TGBTC Discord, November 15, 2026"},{"text":"Record (our call of November 17, these rounds have ended): Spenders, by priority (not date order): LR Tactic chest, Promotion Stones, Full Score Cells, Potential Lucky Coins, Advanced Scene Cores (both rounds, November 18 and 22). The Potential Lucky Coin round ends November 17 at 8:00 PM US Eastern. All of that costs 37,800 Diamonds at the lowest price (30,300 without the Lucky Coins), or 46,800 with the Panacean Refinement Crystal. The game says it \"enables any character to achieve Skill Refinement\"; one of our players reports that only 6★ characters can be refined. (player report)","source":"our call from the prices in game event table ActGroupBuy_Anniv_2nd (Broken Chains copy of the game tables, pulled November 4, 2026); game item text of the Panacean Refinement Crystal (item 20203); refining needs 6★: a player report of November 16, 2026"},{"text":"Each Promotion Stone casket lets you pick 1 Character Exclusive Promotion Stone, \"used to promote a character to MR\". We think these are the stones a character needs past level 200; another org calls them level 350 stones. (our reading) At 1,800 Diamonds for 30 caskets, this is the cheapest round in the event.","source":"game event table ActGroupBuy_Anniv_2nd (Broken Chains copy of the game tables, pulled November 4, 2026); game item text ItemDesc_20419 (the casket); the level 200 step is in the card \"Past level 200: Promotion Stones and Crimson Crystals\" on this page (in-game screenshot, November 14, 2026)"},{"text":"Do not spend Diamonds you saved for your next Carnival guarantee on the optional rounds.","source":"our call"}],"table":{"head":["Round","When","You get","Full price","Lowest price","Our call"],"rows":[["19","November 22, first half","Advanced Scene Core Selection ×4","10,000","5,000","Buy if Diamonds are left"],["20","November 22, second half","Exclusive Treasure Box Key ×100","10,000","5,000","Skip"],["21","November 23","Panacean Refinement Crystal ×1","12,000","9,000","Only with a 6★ (player report)"]],"note":"Prices are in Diamonds. \"Lowest price\" is what the round costs after every discount step; the difference from what you paid is mailed back if the round reaches its last step (our reading: the game fills it by itself).","source":"game event table ActGroupBuy_Anniv_2nd (Broken Chains copy of the game tables, pulled November 4, 2026); the \"Our call\" column is our call; both must-buys are also \"Buy 100%\" in a buy list shared by another org (screenshot in the TGBTC Discord, November 16, 2026), which is looser than us on the optional rounds"},"verify":"Status when this guide was built: both must-buy rounds (November 19 and 21) have ended. Rounds that have ended are listed in the card \"2nd Anniversary Value Group Buy: rounds already over\" below; the lines below that name them are kept as a record."},{"id":"lr-cells","top":true,"title":"LR cells: how you get them (the Cell Creation event)","intro":"An LR cell is an Rc Cell made for one character. The one source we know of is a weekend event called Cell Creation. One creator explains the rules; lines marked \"game text\" quote the event screen itself.","lines":[{"text":"Your place on the ranking comes from your Personal Points in the current round. Each pull costs 1 Cell Creation coin and gives 10 points. Nothing on the screen or in the video ties the ranking to combat power or Arena rank. (game text, creator tip)","source":"Aslan, Cell Creation guide (October 10, 2026)"},{"text":"The board mixes players from several servers. On one screen the ranked players carry the tags FR001, FR016, FR009 and FR015, and the creator watching it is on DE008. So being first on your own server does not put you first here. (seen on a creator's screen)","source":"the event screen in Aslan's video (October 10, 2026), frame at 4:18"},{"text":"The top 3 of each round each get one of the 6 LR cells on show. Game text: \"Top 3 in each round must receive exclusive cells\". Which of the 6 you get is random, so first place can get the one nobody wants. (game text, creator tip)","source":"game text on the event screen (frame at 4:18) and Aslan's explanation (October 10, 2026)"},{"text":"The cells that are left are raffled among everyone lower down. To get any cell from a round, top 3 included, you need 100 points in that round (10 pulls). Game text: \"Participation Requirement: Reach 100 Personal Points in this round\". (game text, creator tip)","source":"game text on the event screen (frame at 4:18) and Aslan's explanation (October 10, 2026)"},{"text":"A round ends when everyone's pulls together reach 20,000 points, which is 2,000 pulls. Then a new round starts. The screen shows it as \"Heat reached 6770/20000\". (game text, creator tip)","source":"game text on the event screen (frame at 4:18) and Aslan's explanation (October 10, 2026)"},{"text":"The slow way: each round pays Cell Fluid by rank, 500 for 1st, 400 for 2nd and 300 for 3rd. The creator thinks 4th and 5th get 200 and 6th to 10th get 100, but says he is not sure. 1,000 Cell Fluid buys an LR cell in the Cell Shop. The video does not show whether you can pick which one. The event rules only say Cell Fluid is sent by ranking; the amounts are from the creator's memory. (creator tip)","source":"Aslan, Cell Creation guide (October 10, 2026)"},{"text":"How many pulls it took on that screen, part-way through a round: 71 for 3rd place, 76 for 2nd and 161 for 1st. Your server group will be different. (seen on a creator's screen)","source":"the event screen in Aslan's video (October 10, 2026), frame at 4:18"},{"text":"The event runs on Saturday and Sunday, about every two weeks. The creator thinks you get 3 free coins a day, plus one free single pull every 24 hours; more coins come from the Pack button for Diamonds or money. (creator tip)","source":"Aslan, Cell Creation guide (October 10, 2026)"},{"text":"Our call: a top-3 place gets you one of the 6 cells at random. On that screen 3 of the 6 were the new cell, so it is about a coin flip, not a sure thing. Only race when any of the 6 would help you. Otherwise, if you will reach 100 points (10 pulls) in a round anyway, you join that round's raffle for the cells the top 3 did not get. Nobody knows how many players share that raffle, and the free coins may not cover 10 pulls, so we would not buy coins just to enter it. Each new round needs another 100 points. Keep \"High-Rating Cells UP\" selected; the creator says the other filters did not help. The creator also says any pull has a small chance to drop one of the cells shown under the Exclusive Cell button (creator tip, unconfirmed). (our call, creator tip)","source":"our call; the filter tip is Aslan's (October 10, 2026)"},{"text":"Not known yet: the Diamond price of one coin, and when the event first opens on a new server. One creator says LR cells unlock 3 to 4 months into a server; another says it takes 3 to 5 months to get one (creator tips, unconfirmed). Our server opened October 16, 2026 (our own record), so November 18 was day 34. That Wednesday the Event menu did not list Cell Creation; it is a weekend event, so that does not settle it. (creator tip, seen in game)","source":"Aslan, beginner guide (October 25, 2026): \"3 to 5 months\"; Kitcat (September 8, 2026): \"3 to 4 months\"; the Event menu of one of our accounts on November 18, 2026"}]},{"id":"exchange-prices","top":false,"title":"Exchange shops: every price we could see","intro":"Six of the ten Exchange tabs show almost all their prices to a free, low-VIP account (Organization hides four rows until Organization Tech Tier 8; Crystal hides one row that is not unlocked yet). Real-Time Arena shows two open rows and VIP one; the rest need a rank or a VIP level. Premium Monthly Card hides every price without the card. Salvage is locked.","lines":[{"text":"Cell Evolution Eukaryote costs 500 Diamonds each on the Regular tab, and 200 Limit Crystals for 10 (20 each) on the Limit Crystal tab (15 times a week). Our call: buy it with Limit Crystals, not Diamonds. (seen in game, our call)","source":"the prices are from the Exchange screens (November 18, 2026); the advice is our call"},{"text":"The Crystal tab sells a Panacean Star-Up Crystal for 1 UR Crystal and a Selection SSR Character for 8 SSR Crystals. One SSR Crystal also buys 50 Limit Crystals. A Talent Certificate ×30,000 row (2 a week) was marked to unlock on November 19; its price was not shown yet. (seen in game)","source":"Exchange screens of one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (every tab, scrolled to the end)"},{"text":"Free, and it looks daily: a Regular Battery on the Crystal tab and 1,000,000 Gold on the VIP tab. Both showed Sold Out when we looked, with a timer of about 8¾ hours to the next one. (seen in game)","source":"Exchange screens of one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (every tab, scrolled to the end)"},{"text":"Organization tab: four more rows open with Organization Tech Tier 8. Level 1 opens Gold ×3,000,000 (5 a week), level 2 Exclusive Treasure Box Key ×5 (5 a week), level 3 Potential Lucky Coin ×5 (2 a week) and level 4 Event Summon Ticket ×5 (2 a week). Their prices are hidden until then. (seen in game)","source":"Exchange screens of one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (every tab, scrolled to the end)"},{"text":"VIP tab, what each level opens (prices hidden below that level): VIP 6 Promotion Crystal III and Gold ×1,500,000, 5 a day each. VIP 7 Free Diamonds once a day and Event Summon Ticket ×5 once a week. VIP 8 a Summon Ticket and Exclusive Treasure Box Key ×10, once a day each. VIP 9 Event Summon Ticket ×10 and Cell Promoter ×100, once a week each. VIP 10 a Panacean Star-Up Crystal once a month and Cell Evolution Eukaryote ×30 once a week. VIP 11 a Panacean Refinement Crystal twice a month. VIP 12 opens a Shachi Random Ability Sphere 3 times a week, VIP 13 another one 5 times a week, and VIP 15 a third Shachi row (no limit shown). (seen in game)","source":"Exchange screens of one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (every tab, scrolled to the end)"},{"text":"Premium Monthly Card Shop (only while the card is active): Free Diamonds, a Summon Ticket, Limit Crystal ×5, Exclusive Treasure Box Key ×5 and Gold ×2,000,000 once a day each; Event Summon Ticket ×5 once a week; a Panacean Star-Up Crystal and Event Summon Ticket ×10 once a month. Prices are hidden without the card. (seen in game)","source":"Exchange screens of one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (every tab, scrolled to the end)"},{"text":"Real-Time Arena tab: the best rows need a rank. Master V opens a Panacean Star-Up Crystal (once a month), a Random UR cell (Score 100) once a week, Special Fragment Selection Chest VII (10 a week), the Superlative Potential Box (2 a week), an Attribute Material Selection Chest (no limit shown) and an Initial Fragment Selection Chest (2 a day). Diamond V opens Panacean Star-Up Crystal Shard ×15 once a week. Platinum V opens an Initial Fragment Selection Chest (1 a day) and a Random Initial Character Fragment (5 a day). Open to everyone: Talent Certificate ×100 for 100 Real-Time Arena points and a Random Initial Character Fragment for 50 (3 a day). (seen in game)","source":"Exchange screens of one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (every tab, scrolled to the end)"}],"table":{"head":["Shop tab","Item","Price","Limit"],"rows":[["Regular","Panacean Crystal Nucleus ×1","5,000 Diamonds","1 per day"],["Regular","Random Full Score UR Factor Attribute Cell ×1","10,000 Diamonds",""],["Regular","Random Full Score UR Factor Attribute Cell ×1","100,000,000 gold","1 per week"],["Regular","Cell Evolution Eukaryote ×1","500 Diamonds",""],["Regular","Nuclear Battery ×1","500 Diamonds",""],["Regular","Improved Battery ×1","100 Diamonds","sold out when we looked; came back in about 8¾ hours (looks daily)"],["Regular","Premium Bond Tablet (Yellow, Blue or Red) ×10","500 Diamonds",""],["Regular","Strength Data, Speed Data or Skill Data ×500","500 Diamonds",""],["Regular","Gold ×2,000,000","500 Diamonds",""],["Regular","Bond Tablet (Yellow, Blue or Red) ×10","50 Diamonds",""],["Regular","Sweep Coupon ×1","50 Diamonds",""],["Regular","Assignment Refresh Coupon ×1","30 Diamonds","10 per day"],["Regular","Promotion Stone, WIT / PSY / DST, 5★ / 4★ / 3★ / 2★ / 1★ (each)","80 / 40 / 20 / 10 / 5 Diamonds",""],["Friendship Point","Promotion Crystal III ×1","2,500 Friendship Points","1 per day"],["Friendship Point","Gemstone Bunny ×1","800 Friendship Points","1 per day"],["Friendship Point","Combat Manual - Advanced ×1","800 Friendship Points","1 per day"],["Friendship Point","Improved Battery ×1","500 Friendship Points","5 per day"],["Friendship Point","4-star Promotion Stone (STR, SKL or SPD) ×1","400 Friendship Points","5 per day"],["Friendship Point","Bond Tablet (Red, Yellow or Blue) ×5","300 Friendship Points","10 per day"],["Friendship Point","Potential Stone ×10","200 Friendship Points","10 per day"],["Friendship Point","Sweep Coupon ×1","50 Friendship Points","20 per day"],["Friendship Point","Promotion Stone, WIT / PSY / DST, 5★ / 4★ / 3★ / 2★ / 1★ (each)","160 / 80 / 40 / 20 / 10 Friendship Points",""],["Crystal","Panacean Star-Up Crystal ×1","1 UR Crystal",""],["Crystal","Selection Special Character ×1","3 UR Crystals",""],["Crystal","Random Rainbow Potential Lv.6 ×1","2 UR Crystals","1 per week"],["Crystal","Selection SSR Character ×1","8 SSR Crystals",""],["Crystal","Lv.4 Random Potential ×1","1 SSR Crystal",""],["Crystal","Limit Crystal ×50","1 SSR Crystal",""],["Crystal","Regular Battery ×1","Free","sold out when we looked; came back in about 8¾ hours (looks daily)"],["Crystal","Special Character Fragment Chest ×1","3 SR Crystals","2 per day"],["Crystal","Lv.3 Random Potential ×1","3 SR Crystals",""],["Crystal","Sweep Coupon ×10","3 SR Crystals","10 per week"],["Crystal","Limit Crystal ×5","1 SR Crystal",""],["Crystal","Crimson Crystal ×30","1 SR Crystal",""],["Crystal","4-star Promotion Stone (STR, SKL or SPD) ×10","1 SR Crystal",""],["Crystal","Improved Battery ×1","3 R Crystals","sold out when we looked; came back in about 8¾ hours (looks daily)"],["Crystal","Limit Crystal ×1","1 R Crystal",""],["Crystal","Combat Manual - Intermediate ×3","1 R Crystal",""],["Crystal","Gold ×600,000","1 R Crystal",""],["Arena","Character piece ×1: Noro [Quick Revival], Yakumo Omori [Jason], Naki [Crybaby] or Nico [Ladyboy in Love]","3,000 Arena points",""],["Arena","Limit Crystal ×10","100 Arena points",""],["Arena","Sweep Coupon ×5","50 Arena points","sold out when we looked; came back in about 8¾ hours (looks daily)"],["Arena","Promotion Stone, WIT / PSY / DST, 5★ / 4★ / 3★ / 2★ / 1★ (each)","48 / 24 / 12 / 6 / 3 Arena points",""],["Organization","Character piece ×1: Iwao Kuroiwa [Arata proto], Yukinori Shinohara [Arata proto], Kureo Mado [Quinque Maniac] or Kohtaro Amon [Twinblades of Justice]","10,000 Organization notes","1 per week"],["Organization","Crimson Crystal ×30","500 Organization notes","5 per week"],["Organization","Limit Crystal ×10","200 Organization notes","20 per week"],["Organization","Promotion Stone, WIT / PSY / DST, 5★ / 4★ / 3★ / 2★ / 1★ (each)","80 / 40 / 20 / 10 / 5 Organization notes",""],["Limit Crystal","Cell Evolution Eukaryote ×10","200 Limit Crystals","15 per week"],["Limit Crystal","Legendary Enhancement Stone ×10","150 Limit Crystals","2 per week"],["Limit Crystal","Apex Enhancement Stone ×10","100 Limit Crystals","10 per week"],["Limit Crystal","Cell Promoter ×10","80 Limit Crystals","50 per week"],["Limit Crystal","Scarlet, Yellow or Azure Core II ×5","75 Limit Crystals",""],["Limit Crystal","Fine Enhancement Stone ×10","50 Limit Crystals",""],["Limit Crystal","Rare Enhancement Stone ×10","25 Limit Crystals",""],["Limit Crystal","Scarlet, Yellow or Azure Core I ×5","15 Limit Crystals",""],["Limit Crystal","Normal Enhancement Stone ×10","10 Limit Crystals",""],["Limit Crystal","4-star Promotion Stone (WIT, PSY or DST) ×1","4 Limit Crystals",""],["Real-Time Arena","Talent Certificate ×100","100 Real-Time Arena points",""],["Real-Time Arena","Random Initial Character Fragment ×1","50 Real-Time Arena points","3 per day"],["VIP","Gold ×1,000,000","Free","sold out when we looked; came back in about 8¾ hours (looks daily)"]],"note":"A blank limit means the screen showed none. Prices are what one of our accounts (level 74, low VIP) saw on November 18, 2026; the Exchange opens from the bar at the bottom of the home screen.","source":"Exchange screens of one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (every tab, scrolled to the end)"}},{"id":"faction-ranking","top":true,"title":"Which org is strongest right now (player vs player)","intro":"Power on paper is almost equal, so the kits decide. This is the order for Arena and Stronghold in November 2026, based mostly on one player on older servers. Bosses are a different story: see the last line.","lines":[{"text":"1. Anteiku. A player on two older servers says it wins most there, and that it works at 1 to 3 stars. It bursts No Organization teams down on turn one, even ones 200,000 to 300,000 CP above it. (player report)","source":"one player on two older servers, TGBTC Discord, November 16, 2026 (player report)"},{"text":"2. Aogiri Tree. Second on those servers, and about half of the top 10 on an old server we checked (our estimate; most teams were hidden). It needs heavy investment: the top team needs its LR cells, the units alone are not enough. (player report, creator tip)","source":"one player on two older servers, TGBTC Discord, November 16, 2026; our own check of an old server's top 10; Aslan (October 8, 2026): \"having these units alone is not enough\""},{"text":"3. CCG (our placement: the one player asked was unsure, and CCG ranked near the top in the past). Few top players run it on his servers (the CCG player he mentions sits around rank 20), so it is the least proven. A creator found Hideyoshi plus Juzo CCG teams very strong against Aogiri defenses. (player report, creator tip)","source":"a player on an older server, TGBTC Discord, November 16, 2026; Aslan (October 26, 2026)"},{"text":"4. No Organization. It does not survive Anteiku's opening burst right now, even with more CP. One player thinks this will change once Uta [The Past] gets an LR cell. (player report)","source":"one player on two older servers, TGBTC Discord, November 16, 2026 (player report)"},{"text":"On old servers with LR cells the picture changes. Aslan said on November 3, 2026 that \"no org is just so OP\", and his November 15 tier list has top-tier characters in every org: Yoshimura [Owl of Readiness] and Hinami [Halloween] for Anteiku, Noro, Naki and Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri] for Aogiri Tree, Sen with her LR cell for No Organization. His list counts LR cells. So the order above is for young servers like ours, before LR cells. (creator tip, our reading)","source":"Aslan (November 3 and November 15, 2026); character names matched from his nicknames by us"},{"text":"Power does not separate the orgs. Average top-level power: No Organization 168,218, Aogiri Tree 167,975, Anteiku 167,490, CCG 166,366. Best five characters, averaged (2026 Q4): Aogiri Tree 180,721, CCG 180,467, Anteiku 180,026, No Organization 178,359. The gap is 1.1% to 1.3%.","source":"our data book, game data SEA 13368 (average top-level power of every SSR and UR; best five per org)"},{"text":"Creators run all four: of 33 team screens, 10 are Anteiku, 10 Aogiri Tree, 7 No Organization and 6 CCG.","source":"33 team screens from 9 creators, December 2025 to October 2026"},{"text":"For bosses and the Weekly Challenge, test your strongest team first, whatever its org (our advice). Our best Big Madam and Weekly Challenge scores used Nutcracker (No Organization) as the finisher.","source":"our own boss tests, October 28 and November 3, 2026"}]},{"id":"force-talents-numbers","top":true,"title":"Force Talents: what each branch gives and what to buy first","intro":"Force Talents are bought with Talent Certificates. Each org has its own tree, and a tree only helps characters of that org. The stat values of the first 37 nodes are the same for all four orgs; only the star requirements and the character nodes differ.","source":"game text FactionTalent_Tips_4 (\"Insufficient Talent Certificates\") and item 20242 \"Talent Certificate\"","lines":[{"text":"Buy in this order: your main team's org first. Inside it: the middle branch (flat stats), then the top branch (% stats). Character nodes come last, and only for characters you really use. (creator tip)","source":"Shi (March 23 and May 21, 2026), Aslan (May 25, 2026), Zeketta"},{"text":"The fullest creator walk-through: on your main org, the middle branch up to Damage Reduction, then the whole top branch, then finish Damage Reduction. Next, the character nodes of your main team, but only for characters at SSS. Then the middle branch of every other org up to ATK Boost IV. A unit from another org in your team (Hideyoshi is No Organization) only gets its own org's talents, so raise that org next. Then the Damage Dealt nodes of your main org (before No Organization if Hideyoshi is not in your main team). Your second team comes last. (creator tip)","source":"Black_Assasine12, Force Talent guide (December 1, 2025); the same order in short from Shi (March 23 and May 21, 2026), Aslan (May 25, 2026) and Zeketta"},{"text":"Middle branch, the first 19 nodes (flat stats): ATK +3,200, DEF +3,200 and HP +64,000 for every character of that org. No star requirement: a middle node only needs the node before it (in-game screen in a creator video of December 1, 2025).","source":"game files of September 22, 2026 (Force Talent text and value table)"},{"text":"Top branch, all 18 nodes: +12% each to Block Chance, Lifesteal, PEN Rate, CRIT DEF, Regeneration Rate, CRIT Rate, CRIT Resist, Restoration Rate and CRIT DMG (two nodes per stat, 5% then 7%).","source":"game files of September 22, 2026 (Force Talent text and value table)"},{"text":"The top branch opens with stars: each node needs a total number of stars across your characters of that org. The whole branch is open at 48 stars for No Organization, 60 for Anteiku, 70 for Aogiri Tree and 140 for CCG.","source":"game text of September 22, 2026"},{"text":"So stars on any character of your org count, not only your main team. Cheap stars on characters you do not field still open nodes for the ones you do. (our reading of the game text)","source":"game text of September 22, 2026"},{"text":"After ATK Boost VI the middle branch goes on with Damage Taken Reduction nodes, and after CRIT DMG Boost II the top branch goes on with Damage Dealt Increase nodes: 0.5% a node, and each top node needs more org stars (in-game screens in a creator video of December 1, 2025). In our files the star-gated nodes run on to 126 stars for No Organization, 180 for Anteiku, 189 for Aogiri Tree and 260 for CCG. One price is visible in that video: 30,000 Talent Certificates for BLK Chance Boost I.","source":"game text of September 22, 2026"},{"text":"Character nodes: each one needs you to own two named characters, and it boosts only that character: +1% damage, then +7% damage and -7% damage taken once the character is SS, and +8% and -8% at SSS (in-game screen in a creator video of December 1, 2025). That is why creators only buy these for SSS characters.","source":"game text of September 22, 2026"},{"text":"Rough value: 50,000 Talent Certificates spent gives about 2,500 CP, and it scales in a straight line. Creators call the certificates \"Force Talents\" or \"papers\". (creator tip)","source":"Shi (April 27, 2026); \"papers\": Zeketta"}]},{"id":"lr-tactics","top":true,"title":"LR Tactics: which ones to take","intro":"A character has 3 Tactic slots: at level 1, level 250 and level 265 (game setting TacticHeroWearMax). This follows the newest creator tier list (November 16, 2026); where an older video disagrees, we say so.","lines":[{"text":"From the LR Tactic Selection Chest, take Fortify. Aslan calls it the safe pick (\"you can't do anything wrong\"), Shi ranks it S tier, and three creators put Fortify on every character. Second choice: Potent Tactic. (creator tip)","source":"Aslan (November 16, 2026), Shi (April 3 and April 28, 2026), Soul (June 19, 2026), Aslan (July 22, 2026)"},{"text":"Healing Prohibition Tactic has dropped. Aslan says he used to rate it really good and now puts it at mid or trash (\"not really needed anymore\"), because many characters already cut healing. One player on an older server still picks it first, and Aslan himself used it against Aogiri Tree in early 2026. (creator tip, player report)","source":"Aslan (November 16, 2026; earlier: February 15 and March 23, 2026); a player on an older server, TGBTC Discord, November 15, 2026"},{"text":"Continuous ATK depends on your team, and it is only a 20% chance. Good on No Organization (Sen heals the team when it triggers; a viewer added Uta and Rize, and Aslan agreed) and on CCG's newest Haise. On Anteiku maybe only on Toka [School Festival Maid Costume]. Not worth it on Aogiri Tree right now. Shi ranked it S tier in April. (creator tip)","source":"Aslan (November 16, 2026); Shi (April 3, 2026)"},{"text":"Good to pull from an LR Tactic Random Chest: Guaranteed CRIT (one of Aslan's top-rated Tactics, because so many characters hit with follow-up attacks), Shield Tactic, Fortified Armor Tactic, Power Strike Tactic, Roulette Tactic, Assistance Tactic and Priority Protection. Repeated Strike is good on Anteiku, whose characters are mostly Balance type. (creator tip)","source":"Aslan, LR Tactic tier list (November 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Weak in the same list: Killing Tactic, Chain Strikes, Momentum Strike and Provocation Counter. Burst-type Tactics are held back because almost no Burst characters are played. Group Upgrade can work on Aogiri Tree. In February, Shi still wanted one Provocation Counter on the field. (creator tip)","source":"Aslan (November 16, 2026); Shi (February 13, 2026)"},{"text":"Assistance Tactic belongs on your back-up: its text says it also works from the back-up slot, and Shi says it is the only Tactic that does. (creator tip)","source":"game text SkillDesc_Tactic017_zy6; Shi (April 3, 2026)"},{"text":"Each LR Tactic read out in the video also gives all stats and Damage Reduction Rate +4% on top of its effect. Some LR effects changed after our game files of September 22, 2026 (Potent Tactic and Redemption read differently in the November video), so check the in-game text before you choose.","source":"in-game Tactic text read aloud in Aslan's video (November 16, 2026); in-game screenshot of November 14, 2026"},{"text":"Ten Tactics exist only as LR: Continuous ATK, Redemption, Weak Bonus-Attack, Guaranteed CRIT, Repeated Strike, Chain Strikes, Primed and Ready, Priority Protection, Group Upgrade and Momentum Strike. (our reading: the game text has only an LR entry for them)","source":"game text of September 22, 2026"},{"text":"Spare Tactics are not wasted: crafting uses 3 Tactics, and three of the same quality (SR, SSR or UR) have a 10% chance to give a higher quality. A UR or LR Tactic can also be refined into a random Tactic of the same quality for 5,000 (UR) or 20,000 (LR) Diamonds; we would not pay that. (our opinion)","source":"game settings TacticHeroWearMax, TacticCompNeedAmount, TacticRefineCost and game text TacticUI_18, TacticCompose_RuleDesc_1_0_2 (files of September 22, 2026)"}]},{"id":"events-free-vs-paid","top":false,"title":"Event pages: what is free and where the money buttons are","intro":"Seen on our own accounts on November 18, 2026, on a server about five weeks old. Event names and prices can differ on your server.","lines":[{"text":"Chain Campaign Boost and Endless Trial Boost (Event menu) each have a free top row: 100 Diamonds for every depth step you have reached, and one tap claims them all. The row under it costs 24.99 USD. One of our accounts had 300 and 400 Diamonds waiting on the two pages, and another had 1,200. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on two of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshots)"},{"text":"Lucky Wheel, Value Pack page: one Free pack a day (1 wheel ticket) sits beside packs of 0.99 to 14.99 USD. We saw a 0.99 USD pack move into the same spot after the claim (seen once, on one account). Our call: tap once and look before you tap again. (seen in game, our call)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Lucky Wheel Point Shop: the first item is 100 Diamonds for 1 cake token, 10 times. Our call: buy that first. Spending 10 tokens opens phase 2 (Potential Lucky Coins, an exclusive ticket); later phases open at 50, 150 and 450 tokens spent. (seen in game, our call)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Potential Wheel: a spin costs 1 Potential Lucky Coin. When your coins run out, the same two buttons switch to 100 and 1,000 Diamonds. Our call: check the price on the button before each press. (seen in game, our call)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Wheel of Fortune (Event menu) spins cost real money, 0.29 USD each. Diamond Spring takes 500 Diamonds or 4.99 USD. The 2nd Anniversary Special Sign-In has one free row; its second and third rows open only after a 9.99 USD purchase. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Exclusive Treasure Box keys: on the event page each Open press spends 1 key. The Assistant tab \"Open Exclusive Ability Sphere\" spends them in batches; one press used 88 keys. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Card Treasure Hunt: each stage has 30 face-down cards and one hides the stage prize. Stage 4's prize is 1,000 Diamonds. Flips: you start with 15, daily quests give 1 or 2 each (one of them, \"obtain 10 paid-currency points\", needs a purchase), and these goals give 5 each: log in 4 and 7 days, finish Force Challenge 5 times (it counts once per arc per day) and take part in 20 Conquest Battles. Moving to the next stage throws away the cards you did not flip. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Character Activity, BOSS Challenge: you need the event character in your line-up, and you can borrow a friend's copy. Borrowed damage scores 50%. One AUTO run with a level 300 team and a borrowed copy scored 57,156 and opened every point tier at once, 800 Diamonds among them. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"}]},{"id":"daily-time-savers","top":false,"title":"Daily routine: time savers and traps","intro":"Seen on our own accounts on November 18, 2026 (level 73 to 74, on a server about five weeks old).","lines":[{"text":"The Assistant (a subscription) has a Daily tab with One-click Execute. One press ran Anteiku, the Boss dispatch, the Assignment claims and the Bingo submit. It left four dailies undone: obtain 3 Rc Cells, clear Gold once, clear EXP once and give 1 Bingo Card. Its Gold and EXP sweep rows were set to 0, which likely explains two of them. Our call: do those four by hand. (seen in game, our call)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Daily Activeness chests sit at 20, 40, 60, 80, 100, 120 and 150 points. Quest values we saw: log in 15, clear Gold 15, clear EXP 15, salvage an Rc Cell 15, obtain 3 Rc Cells 10, give a Bingo Card 10, one Exclusive Equipment draw 10. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Rc Cells: on Character, Train, Rc Cells, One-Tap Equip puts the best spare cells on that character with no confirmation. Our call: do it for every character you own first; it should raise combat power. Then use Rc Salvage, Batch, and tick N, R, SR and SSR. On one account 509 leftover cells gave 13.77 million gold and 750 Diamonds. (seen in game, our call)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Do not let the Rc Cell bag and the mailbox fill up together. A full bag sends rewards to the mailbox as \"Inventory Items Overflowed\" mails that last about 30 days, and the mailbox holds 100 mails. With both full, new rewards have nowhere to go. One of our accounts had both full. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"On a line-up screen, One-Tap Promotion raises every unit shown by up to 5 levels per press while your materials last, with no confirmation. Using Quick Upgrade and One-Tap Promotion together took five units from level 200 to 300; there both buttons lost their red dot, which looks like the cap for now. It cost about 155 million gold plus EXP items and no Diamonds; that line-up went from 644,548 to 773,966 CP. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Stamina items: Regular Battery +30, Improved Battery +100, Nuclear Battery +300. The refill box also has a \"Go to Buy\" button for a real-money pack. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Weekly Challenge: one AUTO win at Difficulty 6 (recommended 350,000 CP, 300% score bonus, 20 stamina) with a 510,614 CP team scored 128,859 and opened every reward tier up to 50,000 in one claim: 1,300 Diamonds, 10 keys and 5 million gold among them. Our call: if you do nothing else in your org this week, do one run. (seen in game, our call)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"A Conquest Battle Invitation (red WARNING box with Quit, Suspend and Go) can pop up over any screen when an org member invites you. Go puts you in with a separate Conquest line-up, not your main team. Ours was 1.29 million CP against a 1.6 million boss and lost. Our call: press Quit unless you have set that line-up. The Card Treasure Hunt goal counts Conquest Battles you take part in, so a declined invitation should not count toward it (our reading). (seen in game, our call)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"}]},{"id":"modes-seen-in-game","top":false,"title":"Modes by the numbers: costs, limits and unlocks we saw","intro":"Seen on our own accounts on November 18, 2026 (level 73 to 74, Chain Campaign depth 251 to 265). Numbers change with your depth and level.","lines":[{"text":"Chain Campaign: you get 25 Chain Licenses a day, reset at 05:00 on the game clock. Each Start also costs 30 stamina. A stage at depth 251 needs 5 teams, and Start is refused if any team is empty (\"Add at least one character to your main line-up\"). Auto-Repeat ran all 25 licenses hands-off and took one account from depth 251 to 265, with 1,460 Diamonds in the rewards. That run also used 6 Regular Batteries; Auto-Repeat Settings has an option to use stamina items by itself, which is the likely cause. Our call: turn it off if you want to keep them. (seen in game, our call)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"On the Chain Campaign line-up screen, a swipe that starts on a portrait drags that unit to another team. To scroll, flick on the CP column instead. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Blockade Breakthrough: you pick 3 buffs per round and they stay until the round resets. Sweep on new enemy nodes unlocks at Chain Campaign depth 300; before that you fight each one. Node 18 is the boss. One account cleared nodes 1 to 15; nodes 16 and up showed a padlock and we do not know why. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Force Challenge: the No Organization arc has no unit restriction and its three stages cost 20, 35 and 60 stamina; Sweep All costs 115 stamina and 3 coupons. The CCG arc takes Anteiku units only. The Anteiku arc takes Aogiri units only and opens on Monday, Thursday and Sunday. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Endless Trial has four ladders: the main one, and Trial STR, Trial SKL and Trial SPD. A trial costs 8 stamina. The Automatic Challenge switch chains trials by itself; on one account it cleared 15 trials in a row and brought 1,500 Diamonds. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Exploration: a unit that falls stays out for the rest of that map, and the game rebuilds your line-up from what is left. Our call: level your team before you start a new map. Map V: 30 enemies at 750,000 CP, 3 stamina each, and 2,300 Diamonds for the first clear. (seen in game, our call)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Arena: 5 tickets a day. The main Arena ranking is finalized at 21:00 UTC-8 and the SPD Arena at 22:00 UTC-8; in US Eastern winter time that is midnight and 1:00 AM (1:00 and 2:00 AM in summer, if the game clock stays on UTC-8). CP can understate a team: a 663,650 CP opponent fielded level 300 to 350 units, each with an Assist partner. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"},{"text":"Organization Boss: the Bonus Phase has reward nodes that are finalized at 08:00, 16:00 and 24:00 on the game clock; tap a node marked Claimable to collect it. At Point level 23 the odds shown were SS 15%, S 25%, A 45% and B 15%. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one of our accounts, November 18, 2026 (screenshot)"}]},{"id":"turn-order","top":true,"title":"Who moves first: the CP Match","lines":[{"text":"The team with the higher CP moves first. The game calls this a CP Match: if your CP is lower, the enemy gets the first move.","source":"game text Guidance_Cplow_1, Guidance_Cplow_2 and SkillDesc_1006_b1p2 (\"Winning the CP Match at the start of combat...\")"},{"text":"So CP matters: raise it on the teams you send against other players (Arena, Stronghold), even though a lower-CP team can still win.","source":"game text Guidance_Cplow_2; a player on an older server said \"CP might not mean much\" (TGBTC Discord #general, November 15, 2026), which the game text contradicts"}]},{"id":"scenes","top":true,"title":"Scene Collection: the All Characters row","lines":[{"text":"All Characters scenes buff every character (one SSR+ scene gives HP +12,500, and +15,000 at UR).","source":"in-game screenshot of the Scene Collection, November 14, 2026"}]},{"id":"level-cap","title":"Level cap by server day (our server)","intro":"Our server's day 1 is October 16, 2026. On another server, count the days from your own day 1.","source":"game data Const HeroLevelMaxServerDaysLimit and SeniorArenaTacticUnlockDays (research notes, future plan, section 5); dates counted from our server's day 1","lines":[{"text":"Day 30 (November 14): level cap 200."},{"text":"Day 42 (November 26): level cap 215."},{"text":"Day 50 (December 4): level cap 225."},{"text":"Day 60 (December 14): level cap 235, and Strategic Arena Tactics open."},{"text":"Day 77 (December 31): level cap 250."},{"text":"Day 98 (January 21, 2027): level cap 265."},{"text":"Day 119 (February 11, 2027): level cap 280."},{"text":"Day 147 (March 11, 2027): level cap 300."},{"text":"Opponents at level 350 come from older or other servers. Our cap rises only on the days above; nothing confirms a jump to 350 here.","source":"game data Const HeroLevelMaxServerDaysLimit; a player's \"level 350 in 4 days\" was his own server's timer (TGBTC Discord #general, November 15, 2026)"}]},{"id":"past-200","title":"Past level 200: Promotion Stones and Crimson Crystals","verify":"Verify in your own Exchange: these costs come from another server's screenshots (November 14, 2026).","lines":[{"text":"To go past level 200, each unit needs, among other materials, 10 of its own Promotion Stones and 1,500 Crimson Crystals.","source":"in-game screenshot of the level 200 upgrade screen; a player on an older server, TGBTC Discord #general, November 15, 2026"},{"text":"Promotion Stones are sold in the Blockade Breakthrough Exchange (Promotion tabs by attribute; PSY, WIT and DST share one tab): 1,500 Blockade Breakthrough Tokens each, up to 10 a week for each unit.","source":"in-game screenshot of the Exchange (Promotion-STR tab); item name: game text ItemName_20376"},{"text":"A team of 5 needs 50 stones: 75,000 Blockade Breakthrough Tokens, plus 7,500 Crimson Crystals.","source":"our math from the two lines above"},{"text":"Save every Blockade Breakthrough Token and Crimson Crystal for this. Don't spend them on anything else. (player report)","source":"a player on an older server, TGBTC Discord #general, November 15, 2026"},{"text":"Before you save for a unit, check that its Promotion Stone is listed in the Exchange. Not every unit has one.","source":"in-game screenshot of the Exchange: the STR tab lists 12 units"}]},{"id":"force-talents","title":"Force Talents: plan before you spend","lines":[{"text":"No way to reset Force Talents is known, so plan before you spend Talent Certificates.","source":"game text of the September 22, 2026 files has no Force Talent reset; a player gave the same warning (TGBTC Discord #general, November 15, 2026)"},{"text":"Order: the middle branch (base stats) first, then the top branch (% stats). Do your main team's faction first, then the others. The character branch at the bottom goes last. (creator tip)","source":"Zeketta (creator video L3LDg1CR4-0, research notes on creator advice, section 4)"}]},{"id":"anniv2-group-buy-past","title":"2nd Anniversary Value Group Buy: rounds already over","intro":"For reference, and for servers that get this event later.","lines":[],"table":{"head":["Round","When","You get","Full price","Lowest price"],"rows":[["1","November 10","Panacean Star-Up Crystal ×1","24,000","18,000"],["2","November 11, first half","Potential Lucky Coin ×100","10,000","5,000"],["3","November 11, second half","Advanced Scene Core Selection ×4","10,000","5,000"],["4","November 12","LR Tactic Random Chest ×1","15,000","10,500"],["5","November 13, first half","Exclusive Treasure Box Key ×100","10,000","5,000"],["6","November 13, second half","Research Sweep Certificate ×2","10,000","5,000"],["7","November 14","Full Score Cell Selection Casket I ×2","16,000","8,000"],["8","November 15, first half","Cell Promoter ×100","8,000","4,000"],["9","November 15, second half","Scene Core ×80","8,000","4,000"],["10","November 16","LR Tactic Selection Chest ×1","50,000","30,000"],["11","November 17, first half","Potential Lucky Coin ×150","15,000","7,500"],["12","November 17, second half","Exclusive Treasure Box Key ×100","10,000","5,000"],["13","November 18, first half","Advanced Scene Core Selection ×4","10,000","5,000"],["14","November 18, second half","Research Sweep Certificate ×2","10,000","5,000"],["15","November 19","LR Tactic Random Chest ×1","15,000","10,500"],["16","November 20","Full Score Cell Selection Casket I ×2","16,000","8,000"],["17","November 21, first half","Character Exclusive Promotion Stone Selection Casket ×30","3,600","1,800"],["18","November 21, second half","Scene Core ×120","12,000","6,000"]],"source":"game event table ActGroupBuy_Anniv_2nd (Broken Chains copy of the game tables, pulled November 4, 2026)"}},{"id":"coming-next","top":false,"title":"Coming next: Hinami Fueguchi [Yotsume] and Juzo (new CCG unit, title not confirmed)","intro":"Two units shown in a creator's leaks video on November 18, 2026. Leaked kits can change before release. The names may change too: the creator was not sure of Hinami's (\"Yotsume, is this her name?\") and reads Juzo's as \"special class investigator\". Each line says what it rests on: the datamine as the creator read it out, a creator's opinion, or our read.","lines":[{"text":"Hinami Fueguchi [Yotsume]: STR, Aogiri Tree, a Balance unit rather than a pure damage dealer. Her banner guarantees her at 200 pulls and comes right after Haise [2nd Anniversary]. (datamine, as the creator read it)","source":"Aslan, leaks video (YouTube UAJ0tBoQjyA, November 18, 2026), 0:04 to 0:27 and 1:42 to 1:58"},{"text":"Her active skill at level 3: Slow on all enemies for 1 turn, DEF −8 and CRIT DEF −20 (read out without a % sign), and Frost damage equal to 265% of ATK to all enemies. Frost: CRIT Rate ×3 and damage dealt +50%. A rank effect turns it into Ultra-Frost: damage dealt +70% (which rank is unclear in the video; it sounds like \"x rank\"). (datamine)","source":"Aslan, leaks video (YouTube UAJ0tBoQjyA, November 18, 2026), 2:05 to 2:43"},{"text":"Danger Sense: each time an ally uses a group skill, she gains 1 stack (CRIT Rate +20%, CRIT DMG +40%), up to 4. The creator guesses that a group skill means an attack on all enemies. At 4 stacks she gains Keen Perception: all stats +10%, and her next active skill uses up all Ultimate energy and makes the other Aogiri ally with the highest starting ATK use an active skill of the same level on the enemy with the lowest HP %. Then Keen Perception ends. (datamine; what \"group skill\" means is the creator's guess)","source":"Aslan, leaks video (YouTube UAJ0tBoQjyA, November 18, 2026), 2:43 to 4:31"},{"text":"More passives: the first time her HP drops below 30%, she gains 4 Danger Sense and uses a level 1 active skill at once. Aogiri allies get +30% basic stats; each Danger Sense gives allies +4% max HP (up to 16); her first Keen Perception gives allies ATK +12. Her last passive: the first time within a turn that she gains Keen Perception, her ATK-related stats get +16 for 1 turn and she deals a 230% Ultra-Frost hit on the enemy with the highest starting ATK; something about her next active skill is changed by 20 (unclear in the video); when Keen Perception ends, the damage she takes from the next skill is cut by 80%. (datamine)","source":"Aslan, leaks video (YouTube UAJ0tBoQjyA, November 18, 2026), 4:31 to 5:57"},{"text":"Juzo (new CCG unit, title not confirmed): SPD, CCG, a support unit, also guaranteed at 200 pulls, coming after Hinami. The leak text says he can lock HP to fend off enemies and protect the whole team. His full kit was not out yet on November 18. (datamine, as the creator read it)","source":"Aslan, leaks video (YouTube UAJ0tBoQjyA, November 18, 2026), 0:34 to 1:15 and 9:15 to 9:45"},{"text":"When: the creator thinks Juzo comes around the start of December. That is his guess, and he does not say for which server, so it is not a date for ours. (creator's guess)","source":"Aslan, leaks video (YouTube UAJ0tBoQjyA, November 18, 2026), 1:35 to 1:42"},{"text":"What creators say so far: Aslan will not rate leaked units any more (he expected Takizawa to be strong, and \"right now no one's using him\"); for now Hinami \"sounds okay, she's not bad\", and he will test her. Of Juzo he says CCG is finally getting its support unit. Zeketta (November 19, 2026) also calls Hinami \"really not bad\"; the only transcript we have of that video is a rough machine translation from French, so we quote nothing else from it. (creator opinion)","source":"Aslan, leaks video (YouTube UAJ0tBoQjyA, November 18, 2026), 6:05 to 6:29 and 9:22 to 9:38; Zeketta, Hinami analysis (YouTube g79v8wKsaUE, November 19, 2026), 6:07 to 6:09 (machine translation)"},{"text":"Our read, not a creator recommendation: no creator in our sources says to pull for either unit yet; neither video tells you to pull. Do not move Diamonds for them until creators have tested them in battle. Hinami's kit leans on other Aogiri units (+30% basic stats for Aogiri allies, an extra active skill from an Aogiri ally), so she looks like a unit for Aogiri teams.","source":"our read, from the leaked kit and the two videos above"}],"verify":"SEA dates are not our server's dates. We have no SEA release date for either unit: our copy of the SEA game data (gluttony.dev, build 13455) does not list them yet. Check the banner in your own game."},{"id":"modes-more-1118","top":false,"title":"Modes: more numbers from the November 18 screens","intro":"Seen in game on our accounts on November 18, 2026 (level 73 to 74, on a server opened October 16, 2026), plus one player's reports, each labelled. Numbers change with your depth and level.","lines":[{"text":"Gold and EXP stages cost half stamina that day: the Gold Start button showed 30 struck through to 15, and EXP 20 to 10. We do not know why. One Gold sweep at Difficulty 9 paid 602,000 gold and 3 EXP items. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Chain Campaign: at stage 251-8 the five battles had enemy CP 393,200, 382,890, 376,400, 348,000 and 199,980. Each battle runs as a Quick Battle that says \"Tap anywhere to end Auto-Battle\", so a tap on the screen stops Auto (our reading of that text). (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"A character can be fielded in only one version per Chain Campaign line-up set. (one player's report)","source":"one player's report (November 2026), not yet checked by a second source"},{"text":"Blockade Breakthrough buffs on offer: ATK +15% with PEN +8%; DEF +15% with Block +8%; a shield of 10% max HP at the start of each turn; Restoration +50% with Regeneration and Lifesteal +20%; and a No Organization buff. Coins: an enemy node at 475,751 CP paid 80, one at 542,350 CP paid 100, and a chest 200. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Endless Trial: Trial STR takes STR, PSY and WIT units only. Each trial dropped 10 materials, 1 Gemstone Bunny, 2 Sweep Coupons and 1,000,000 gold. There is also an EX Stage. A 773,966 CP team won trial 102 (enemy 644,000 CP) on AUTO. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Exploration uses its own Exploration line-up. It starts empty; the Auto button fills it with your five strongest units. Map V also has 17 chests and 7 mystery tiles, and progress rewards at 10, 25, 40, 55, 75 and 100. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"World Boss on November 18 was Kureo Mado, with four daily damage rewards at 3.2 million, 3.5 million, 3.8 million and 4 million damage. The Assistant's run had already claimed all four. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Organization Supply: six coffee orders (for example 20 coffees of any kind, 30 iced coffees, 60 of any kind, 15 lattes, 10 SR or better) and a weekly reward for finishing orders. Orders take Coffee items; with none in stock the picker says \"No eligible items found\". (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"}]},{"id":"daily-more-1118","top":false,"title":"Daily routine: more tips (Assistant, Rc Cells, bag, pop-ups)","intro":"Facts seen in game on November 18, 2026 and a few reports from one player, each labelled. Advice is on its own line, marked \"Our call\".","lines":[{"text":"The Assistant has six tabs: Subscription Benefits, Daily, Assignment, Make Coffee, Open Exclusive Ability Sphere and Exchange. On that account its run used 3 of the 5 daily Arena tickets. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Rc Salvage, Batch: besides N, R, SR and SSR, the filter has UR 86-90, UR 91-95 and UR 96-99; the number on a cell is its rating. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Our call: when you batch-salvage, leave the three UR boxes unticked unless you mean to break UR cells.","source":"our call, from the line above"},{"text":"Each character has three Rc Cell slots: ATK, DEF and HP. One-Tap Equip puts the cells it replaces back in your bag. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Bag, Consumables: Gold Advanced Stone Caskets (random SSR to UR Promotion Stones) can be used 99 at a time. On one account, Use did nothing on 25 Advanced Potential Boxes; most likely the Potential bag was full (our reading). (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Pop-ups: after log-in the game showed a \"Real-Time Arena Open\" notice, then a 0.99 USD Daily Value Recruitment Pack offer. On another account, a 99.99 USD pack pop-up came back every time the home screen loaded. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Our call: close these pop-ups. They are paid offers, not rewards.","source":"our call, from the line above"},{"text":"The Assignment Sale shop tab appears only after the day's assignments are done. (one player's report; the Modes page says a sale can appear around the 9th to 16th Bounty)","source":"one player's report (November 2026), not yet checked by a second source"},{"text":"A real-time Conquest invitation gives the invited player about 1,000 Friendship Points per run, and the host pays 50 stamina. We do not know whether a lost run pays the points too. (one player's report)","source":"one player's report (November 2026), not yet checked by a second source"}]},{"id":"events-more-1118","top":false,"title":"Event menu: more numbers (Treasure Box, Potential Wheel, Diamond Spring, Carnival)","intro":"Seen in game on November 18, 2026 (one account), plus reports from one player, each labelled. Events and prices can differ on your server.","lines":[{"text":"Exclusive Treasure Box: five box tiers (bronze, silver, gold, blue, red). A success can upgrade the next box; a failure adds Lucky Value. You pick one Selection Ability Sphere to aim for; its 99 selections refresh on a timer. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Potential Wheel: each spin and each ten-spin asks you to confirm. 66 Potential Lucky Coins gave only Lv.2 to Lv.4 potential chests, and Fortune Points went from 2,677 to 3,186. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Diamond Spring: the 500-Diamond option has 4 slots and resets about every 2 days. (one player's report)","source":"one player's report (November 2026), not yet checked by a second source"},{"text":"Carnival: on that player's server the first Carnival opened about Tuesday, November 3, 2026 and ended Monday, November 16, so it ran about 2 weeks. The game setting ServerOrderCycle is 35; we do not know what it counts. When the next Carnival starts is not confirmed. (one player's report, game data)","source":"one player's report (November 2026); game constant ServerOrderCycle (game constants, copy of October 28, 2026)"}],"table":{"head":["Key of the day","Price (Diamonds)"],"rows":[["1st to 3rd","Free"],["4th","100"],["5th","150"],["6th","150"],["7th","200"],["8th","200"],["9th","1,000"]],"note":"Exclusive Treasure Box keys, per day: 8 keys cost 800 Diamonds in total, and the 9th alone costs 1,000.","source":"one player's report (November 2026), not yet checked by a second source"}},{"id":"anniv2-seen-1118","top":false,"title":"Seen during the 2nd Anniversary event (November 18, 2026): a record","intro":"A record, not current advice. On November 18 the event hub said \"Event ends in 05d 15h\", and the Value Group Buy in the game's event table ends November 24, 2026 at 05:00 server time. Seen on one account; on a server that gets this event later, prizes may differ.","lines":[{"text":"The hub had six parts: Special Sign-In, Path of Fortune+, Celebration Gift, Special Challenge, Value Group Buy and Lucky Wheel. The free Sign-In row listed, for days 3 to 9: 300 Diamonds, 1 ticket, 5 rings, 5 keys, 2 tickets, 300 Diamonds, 5 rings. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Celebration Gift: a list of Joint Celebration Chests, each free to open; the first gave 3 keys. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Special Challenge (boss Orochi, STR): one rewarded run a day, with its own line-up (Auto fills it) and no stamina cost shown. A level 300 team dealt 62,086,355 damage for 4,753 points. Achievement Rewards count the whole server's progress; they paid 6 × 100 Diamonds, and the phase strip paid 15 phase rewards in a row. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Path of Fortune+ (a dice board): it started with 10 normal dice and 3 precision dice, with 3 rerolls a day. Precision Throw lets you pick the landing tile within 6. Bonus tiles roll a d20: one paid 450, 300 or 150 event tickets for 16+, 12-15 or 1-11. Its shop: Summon Ticket for 1,500 tickets (5 times), Ability Booster ×1000 for 600, Strength, Speed or Skill Data ×100 for 180 each, Gemstone Bunny for 120. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Lucky Wheel: a draw costs 1 wheel ticket (10 for a ten-draw). Wheel quests pay cake points: daily ones (log in, use 100, 200 or 400 stamina) and event ones (use 1,500 to 4,000 stamina). Total-draw milestones sit at 25, 50, 75, 100, 125 and 150. Later Point Shop phases: phase 2 (10 tokens spent) has 3 Potential Lucky Coins for 3 tokens (10 times); phase 4 (150 spent) a Lv.6 potential for 50; phase 5 (450 spent) a Lv.7 potential for 225. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"},{"text":"Value Group Buy, round 14 on November 18: Research Sweep Certificate ×2 at 9,000 Diamonds (the first, 10% discount step), with 1,659 of the 1,750 purchases needed for the next step. The game's event table also puts that step at 1,750. (seen in game, game data)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026; game event table ActGroupBuy_Anniv_2nd, round 14, field discount_count (Broken Chains copy of the game tables, pulled November 4, 2026)"},{"text":"Character Activity for Ayato Kirishima [Rebelwing], which ran at the same time (on November 18 its screen said it ends about November 20): the BOSS Challenge cost 30 stamina, the enemy had 100,000 CP and there were at most 5 rounds; a Single Challenge Reward of 100 Diamonds came once a day; Character Trial was a list of stages with level 160 enemies and the same Ayato requirement. (seen in game)","source":"seen in game on one account, November 18, 2026 (server opened October 16, 2026)"}]},{"id":"team-ultimates","top":false,"title":"Team Ultimate skills: the four named ones, and where their items come from","intro":"From the game text (copy of the game tables of November 4, 2026). The game calls them Ultimate skills.","lines":[{"text":"Kagune Attack, Might of Awaken and Twins' Smite hit one enemy; Co-op hits all enemies. Each deals a share of the ATK of your ally with the highest ATK. (game text)","source":"game text TSkillName_TSkill1 to 4 and TSkillDesc_TSkill1 to 4 (copy of the game tables of November 4, 2026)"},{"text":"Where the game text says you get the items for them: Might of Awaken at Chain Campaign Lv.30; Twins' Smite by clearing Conquest Battle - Yamori on every difficulty; Co-op by clearing Force Challenge - CCG. The text gives no such line for Kagune Attack. (a fifth Ultimate has a description in the game text but no name yet) (game text)","source":"game text TSkillUnlockInfo_TSkill2 to 4 (copy of the game tables of November 4, 2026)"},{"text":"Each Ultimate has a passive to develop. When that passive reaches its limit, Ultimate Skill Refresh opens: each refresh gives a result with a comprehensive rating, which you save or abandon. Auto Refresh stops when a result's rating is not lower than before. (game text)","source":"game text UI_TeamSkillFresh_1 to 32 (copy of the game tables of November 4, 2026)"},{"text":"Our call (no recent creator source): Co-op is the only one that hits every enemy, so raise it first for modes with five enemies.","source":"our call, from the game text above; no recent creator source"}]},{"id":"leveling-reports","top":false,"title":"Stars, refining, gear and story: what one player reports","intro":"Reports from one player on a server that opened October 16, 2026. Not yet checked by a second source.","lines":[{"text":"Gold coins do not star up characters; they only refine 6★ characters (grades D to SSS). Panacean crystals can be turned into gold coins, but not back. (one player's report, November 16, 2026)","source":"one player's report (November 16, 2026), not yet checked by a second source"},{"text":"Sources disagree: the Gem planner page quotes Aslan (June 16, 2026) calling gold coins \"duplicates of golden units\".","source":"Aslan (June 16, 2026), as quoted in this guide's Gem planner (VIP 10 golden coins question)"},{"text":"Our call: until a second source settles it, do not buy gold coins to star up a character.","source":"our call, from the two lines above"},{"text":"Story chapter 15 unlocks at Chain Campaign depth 270. On that player's server, chapter 18 opens November 22, 2026, which is server day 38 by our count. (one player's report)","source":"one player's report (November 2026), not yet checked by a second source"},{"text":"Exclusive Equipment costs more to upgrade at each level: about 2,500 material at low levels, and one level at a tier step cost 28,000. (one player's report)","source":"one player's report (November 2026), not yet checked by a second source"}]},{"id":"org-tech-unlock","top":false,"title":"Org Tech: when it opens","intro":"","lines":[{"text":"Organization Tech unlocks at Organization Level 15. (one player's report) The game text on this page gives the server-day gates for the later tiers.","source":"one player's report (November 2026), not yet checked by a second source"}]},{"id":"anteiku-tank","top":false,"title":"Anteiku tip: Ken Kaneki [Natsu Matsuri] in front (one player's report)","intro":"","lines":[{"text":"His 0★ passive Fortitude puts him in a provocation stance for 2 turns at the start of battle, so all attacks go to him, and he is immune to debuffs and Weak while it lasts. It also gives the whole team +3% basic stats for each Anteiku character on the team, him included (up to 12%) and gives Anteiku allies Resist. (game data)","source":"game data: his passive text SkillDesc_1079_p1 (files of September 22, 2026), as on his character page"},{"text":"One player reports that with him in front, the enemy's opening hits land on him, so Hinami [Halloween]'s one-time save goes to him instead of a weak filler unit, and the damage dealers stay at full HP. Their Arena team: Ken Kaneki [Natsu Matsuri], Toka [Maid], Toka [June Bride], Hinami [Halloween], with Toka [1st Anniversary] in back-up. (one player's report; no recent creator source)","source":"one player's report (October 29, 2026); no recent creator source"},{"text":"Our call: worth a try if you already own him. The provocation lasts only 2 turns.","source":"our call, from the two lines above"}],"verify":"No recent creator source. This is one player's tested team, not a creator ranking."}]},"force_talents":{"title":"Force Talent Guide","intro":"What the tree looks like, the order to buy in, what each row gives, and the numbers for each org. Every claim names where it comes from.","rows":[["1","Middle row","flat ATK, DEF, HP"],["2","Top row","% stats"],["3","Character nodes","bottom row"]],"rows_note":"Numbers and colours as marked on the pictures.","pictures_title":"The tree in four pictures","pictures_intro":"Real in-game screens. Every org has the same three rows; the colours and numbers match the buy order above.","pictures":[{"img":"assets/talents/1_rows.jpg","title":"Three rows","text":"Each org's tree has a middle row (flat ATK, DEF, HP), a top row (% stats) and a bottom row of character nodes. You buy nodes with Talent Certificates."},{"img":"assets/talents/2_damage.jpg","title":"Both rows continue into damage nodes","text":"After ATK Boost VI the middle row becomes Damage Taken Reduction. After CRIT DMG Boost II the top row becomes Damage Dealt Increase. Each node is 0.5%."},{"img":"assets/talents/3_gate.jpg","title":"What locks a node, and one price","text":"A top-row node needs a total number of stars across that org's characters (here 114, 117, 120). A middle-row node only needs the node before it. Gold box: this node costs 30,000 Talent Certificates."},{"img":"assets/talents/4_character.jpg","title":"Character nodes pay off at SS and SSS","text":"A character node gives that one character +1% damage. Gold box: at SS it becomes +7% damage and -7% damage taken, at SSS +8% and -8%."}],"credit":"Screenshots: Black_Assasine12, \"How would I recommend distributing force talents in the hide meta?\" (YouTube, Dec 1, 2025), marked up by us.","order_title":"The order to buy in","order_lines":[["force-talents-numbers",0]],"later_title":"Sources differ on the later steps","later_intro":"The order at the top of this page is the main one. The two lines below go on past it and do not agree with each other. Each is shown once, with its source.","later_lines":[["force-talents-numbers",1],["force-talents",1]],"warn_lines":[["force-talents",0]],"gains_title":"What you get","gains_intro":"The flat and % numbers are the same in all four orgs.","gains":[{"label":"Middle row · first 19 nodes","value":"+3,200 ATK","text":"plus +3,200 DEF and +64,000 HP for every character of that org"},{"label":"Top row · 18 nodes","value":"+12% × 9 stats","names":"Block Chance, Lifesteal, PEN Rate, CRIT DEF, Regeneration Rate, CRIT Rate, CRIT Resist, Restoration Rate, CRIT DMG"},{"label":"Damage nodes","value":"0.5% each","text":"Damage Taken Reduction on the middle row, Damage Dealt Increase on the top row. 20 of each in the video = 10% and 10%."},{"label":"Character node","value":"+8% / -8%","text":"damage dealt and damage taken at SSS. +7% / -7% at SS. Only +1% damage before that."},{"label":"Rough CP value","value":"2,500 CP","text":"per 50,000 Talent Certificates, in a straight line (creator estimate)."}],"gains_source":"Game data: value table and game text, files of Sept 22, 2026. Damage nodes and the character node: in-game screens in the video credited under the pictures. Rough CP value: Shi, Apr 27, 2026.","orgs_title":"Org by org","orgs_intro":"How many stars each org needs, and which partner each team regular's character node asks for. Stars are counted across all of that org's characters.","stars_top_label":"total stars on this org's characters to open the whole top row of % stats","stars_last_label":"stars for the last star-gated damage node in our files","node_head":["Character node","You must also own"],"orgs":[{"id":"anteiku","name":"Anteiku","stars_top":"60","stars_last":"180","nodes":[["Toka [School Festival Maid Costume]","Nishiki Nishio [Senior]"],["Yoshimura [Owl of Readiness]","Toka [Blazewing]"],["Toka [June Bride]","Hinami [Fledgling Butterfly]"],["Hinami [Hina Matsuri]","Toka [Blazewing]"],["Ken Kaneki [√A]","Hinami [Fledgling Butterfly]"],["Toka [Flame Strike]","Ken Kaneki [Book-Lover]"]],"note":"Hinami [Halloween] is newer than our files, so her node is not listed."},{"id":"aogiri","name":"Aogiri Tree","stars_top":"70","stars_last":"189","nodes":[["Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri]","Noro [Quick Revival]"],["Ayato [Black Rabbit]","Naki [Crybaby]"],["Naki [Prisoner]","Yakumo [Jason]"],["Noro [Overpower]","Yakumo [Jason]"],["Miza Kusakari [Triple Blade]","Gagi [Naki's Sidekick]"],["Eto [3M Downloads]","Noro [Quick Revival]"]],"note":"Most partners are old launch units. Make sure you own Yakumo [Jason], Naki [Crybaby] and Noro [Quick Revival]."},{"id":"ccg","name":"CCG","stars_top":"140","stars_last":"260","nodes":[["Juzo [False Girl]","Shinohara [Unyielding Shinohara]"],["Haise [Mentor]","Akira [Rose on the Battlefield]"],["Akira [June Bride]","Kaya [Black Dog]"],["Ginshi Shirazu","Kori Ui [Shining New Star]"],["Urie Kuki","Akira [Rose on the Battlefield]"],["Toru Mutsuki","Take Hirako [Absolute Strength]"]],"note":"The most expensive top row by far. Akira [June Bride] is the back-up in most teams, so the CCG middle row helps almost everyone."},{"id":"noorg","name":"No Organization","stars_top":"48","stars_last":"126","nodes":[["Nutcracker","Kie Muramatsu [Applehead]"],["Uta [The Past]","Ken Kaneki [Book-Lover]"],["Hideyoshi [Best Friend]","Toka [Blazewing]"],["Sen Takatsuki [Elegant Deception]","Hinami [Fledgling Butterfly]"],["Sen Takatsuki [Novelist]","Yoshimura [Non-Killing Owl]"],["Rize [Seaside Carnival Party]","Nashiro [Spotless Shroud]"],["Roma [Mad Clown]","Nishiki Nishio [Senior]"]],"note":"The cheapest top row. Hideyoshi and Roma [Mad Clown] sit in other orgs' teams, so this tree pays off for almost everyone."}],"orgs_source":"Game data: value table and game text, files of Sept 22, 2026","details_title":"The numbers, line by line","sources_title":"Where this comes from","sources_head":["Source","What","What it backs up"],"sources":[["Shi","Mar 23 and May 21, 2026","\"Middle and top row for every single org\"; bottom rows for characters you do not use are \"empty CP\"."],["Aslan","May 25, 2026","\"I upgraded the middle row till damage reduction\" before the other rows."],["Zeketta","Force Talent section of his guide","Middle row first, then the top row, main org first, character row last."],["Shi","Apr 27, 2026","Rough value: 50,000 Talent Certificates is about 2,500 CP, in a straight line."],["Game data","value table and game text, files of Sept 22, 2026","The flat-stat and % numbers, the star totals per org, and which partner each character node needs."]],"unknown_title":"What we do not know yet","unknown":["The price of every node. One price is on screen: 30,000 Talent Certificates for BLK Chance Boost I.","Whether the newer damage nodes (XXI to XL in the newest game files) are also 0.5% each."]}}});
